    body:"<h1>"+name+" predictions and match analysis</h1><p class='lead'>"+overview+"</p><h2>How we assess fixtures</h2><p>Our analysis considers the available fixture information, recent team performance, opponent strength, home and away records, relevant scoring and defensive statistics, verified player availability, tactical match-ups, competition context, market definitions and listed prices. Not every data point is available for every match, and information that has not been verified is not treated as fact.</p><h2>Form needs context</h2><p>A sequence of wins or losses is only a starting point. The quality of opponents, match locations, red cards, schedule congestion and the way goals were created or conceded can change how recent results should be interpreted. Small samples should not be mistaken for permanent team characteristics.</p><h2>Markets and prices</h2><p>Depending on the fixture and available markets, analysis may consider match result (1X2), double chance, goals totals, both teams to score and other clearly defined options. Each market answers a different question. We compare the exact selection with its listed price and avoid treating short odds as certainty.</p><h2>Current fixtures and published editions</h2><p>Competition coverage depends on eligible fixtures and available market information. Visit the <a href='/daily'>daily football board</a> to see whether a current fixture has been included in a published edition. Every published selection displays its fixture, market, kick-off time and listed odds.</p><h2>Competition data and standings</h2><p>Where reliable standings and competition data are available, the <a href='/competitions'>competition directory</a> provides the latest cached table. Tables are data snapshots and may not update at the same moment as a match result; check the displayed update information where provided.</p><h2>Related football analysis</h2><p>Read our guides to <a href='/guides/football-form-analysis'>football form</a>, <a href='/guides/implied-probability'>implied probability</a> and <a href='/guides/how-accumulators-work'>accumulators</a>. Review <a href='/results'>yesterday's results</a> to see recorded outcomes, including wins, losses and pending selections.</p><p class='notice'>18+ only. AccaForge is an information website, not a bookmaker. Football outcomes are uncertain and no selection guarantees a result.</p>"
